			I('The big picture: the verbs you need most bend a little', 'To want, to be able, to ask for, to have, to come: the verbs you need every day are exactly the ones that change their stem. The vowel splits when the stress lands on it: e becomes ie or i, o becomes ue. English has nothing like it, but the pattern is steady, and nosotros never changes. This lesson also gives you <b>tener</b>, which Spanish uses where English uses "to be": you "have" hunger, thirst, cold and years. You will need all of this to order food, make plans and say no politely.<br><b>Quiero un café, pero no puedo dormir después.</b> = I want a coffee, but I cannot sleep afterwards.<br><b>¿A qué hora empieza la película?</b> = What time does the film start?<br><b>Tengo sed y tengo que beber agua.</b> = I am thirsty and I have to drink water.', 'Quiero un café, pero no puedo dormir después. ¿A qué hora empieza la película? Tengo sed y tengo que beber agua.')
